<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuel Rojo del Río y Vieyra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1708–1764</span> · Also known as Manuel Rojo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manuel Rojo del Río y Vieyra was a Mexican-born archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> from 1759 and acting governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> from 1761. When British forces took Manila in October 1762 he signed the capitulation and agreed to a large ransom, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-de-anda-y-salazar">Simón de Anda y Salazar</a> refused to recognise his authority. He died in Manila in 1764.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manuel-rojo-del-rio-y-vieyra.jpg" alt="Manuel Rojo del Río y Vieyra" width="214" height="273" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manuel_Antonio_Rojo_del_Rio_Vera.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
